  "body": {
    "id": "prop:odd-slice-correction",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "In the balanced six-unit margin instance, \\(M_2=M_3=15\\). For \\(k\\in\\{2,3\\}\\) and every \\(\\lambda\\in\\Lambda(f,1/2)\\), \\(A_k(\\lambda)=1/4\\), \\(\\Xi_{kk}(\\lambda)\\ge1/900\\), and therefore \\(\\Sigma_{kk}(r,\\lambda)\\le1/(4r_k)-1/900\\). Thus the diagonal endpoint \\(1/(4r_k)\\) is excluded by every compatible one-shot binary schedule.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "n0",
      "m",
      "S",
      "M",
      "f",
      "lambda",
      "Lambda",
      "Amap",
      "Ximap",
      "r",
      "Sigma"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:compatible-couplings",
      "def:balanced-six-unit-instance",
      "thm:sharp-covariance-set"
    ],
    "justification": "The worked face directly certifies the finite-population correction that killed the previous diagonal angle.",
    "gap": "No cited saturation-design result records the odd-slice integrality facet of the one-shot covariance set.",
    "consumer": "The \\(n_0=6\\), \\(m=(1,2,4)\\) design receipt cannot silently return the infeasible diagonal covariance used by the rejected proposal.",
    "proof_tex": "Here \\(M_2={6\\choose2}=15={6\\choose4}=M_3\\). Every target-cell marginal is Bernoulli on \\(\\{0,1\\}\\) with mean \\(1/2\\), so for \\(k=2,3\\),\n\\[\nA_k(\\lambda)=\\frac1{15}\\sum_{z\\in\\mathcal S_k}\\mathbb E_\\lambda\\{t(z)-1/2\\}^2=1/4.\n\\]\nFor each type, the sum of fifteen numbers in \\(\\{-1/2,1/2\\}\\) is a nonzero odd multiple of \\(1/2\\). Therefore\n\\[\n|g_k(t)|\\ge1/30,\\qquad \\Xi_{kk}(\\lambda)=\\mathbb E_\\lambda g_k(t)^2\\ge1/900.\n\\]\nSubstitution into \\(\\Sigma_{kk}=A_k/r_k-\\Xi_{kk}\\) gives \\(\\Sigma_{kk}(r,\\lambda)\\le1/(4r_k)-1/900\\), so the displayed diagonal endpoint is unattainable.",
